+# Plain names the user reads in figures, decks and captions. One term per line: term<TAB>plain definition.
+# .claude/hooks/send_check.py lets a listed term through (whole word, any case). The user approves every entry.
+dimensionless target	the network's target made free of units: |M|^2 times the product of the event's emission scales (one per leg beyond 2->2), divided by (4 pi alpha_s)^q (4 pi alpha)^e for the process's QCD and QED orders, with momenta and masses given to the network in units of the collision energy sqrt(s_hat)
+context vector	16 learned numbers per training process, added to every particle's encoding and learned with the network (set to zero on half the events); a new process gets zero, or a vector fitted on a few of its events with the network frozen
+catalog_v3	the catalog generated on 2026-10-24: one process per relabelling class, trees up to 2->4 (2->5 as probes), one-loop QCD corrections, loop-induced processes, the strong coupling at 0.09 and 0.15, heavy quarks at 50, 300 and 600 GeV, Z' and two-Higgs-doublet processes; collision energy up to 1 TeV, b quark of 4.7 GeV, transverse momentum above 10 GeV
+catalog_v4	catalog_v3's processes regenerated with wider coverage: collision energy up to 6 TeV drawn uniform in its logarithm, a hadron-collider acceptance (transverse momentum above 10 GeV, pseudorapidity within 5), a share of events turned forward, every tree diagram including the electroweak ones, a massless b quark, the top at 172.5 GeV everywhere
+new combinations	held-out axis H1: processes whose particles all appear in training, in combinations never trained on
+higher multiplicity	held-out axis H2: 2->4 processes of families with no 2->4 member in training; the 2->5 probes are H2.5 (also written H2p5)
+the top	held-out axis H3, particle content: processes with the physical top quark, while heavy quarks with the top's quantum numbers at 50, 300 and 600 GeV are trained; in the twin run also every process with a tau or tau neutrino
+quartic vertex	held-out axis H4, vertex class: processes built on the quartic gauge vertex, held out in the twin run
+one loop	held-out axis H5, perturbative order: one-loop amplitudes of processes whose trees are trained
+strong coupling 0.13	held-out axis H6, parameter interpolation: the strong coupling at 0.13, with 0.09 and 0.15 trained
+energy and cuts	held-out axis H7: a tighter cut, transverse momentum of at least 30 GeV with 10 GeV trained (H7c); and higher collision energy (H7E), 1 to 10 TeV on catalog_v3 (up to 1 TeV trained), 6 to 20 TeV on catalog_v4 (up to 6 TeV trained)
+zero-shot	a held-out process predicted by the pretrained network with nothing trained or fitted on it
+fine-tune	the pretrained network trained further on the events of one new process, all weights, the layers nearest the input at a smaller learning rate (layer decay)
+Muon	the optimizer in use since 2026-10-26: momentum updates orthogonalised on the network's hidden weight matrices, AdamW on the other weights
+AdamW	Adam with decoupled weight decay; the optimizer before Muon
+relabelled processes	held-out processes equal to a training process up to a relabelling of particles (the same |M|^2 up to a constant, for instance one massless quark flavour for another): interpolation
+new processes	held-out processes equal to no training process under any relabelling: extrapolation
+level of the error	with Delta = predicted minus true log|M|^2 over a process's events, the squared mean of Delta: an overall offset
+shape of the error	the variance of Delta over a process's events, what no offset removes; the mean squared error is level plus shape
